{"data": [{"author_id": "1687985018717478912", "created_at": "2026-11-03T01:11:17.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117424339507146875"], "id": "2117424339507146875", "in_reply_to_user_id": "39125788", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 1, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117279363175739630", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@emollick The practical takeaway for companies: train people on the durable skill (delegating, writing a clear spec, checking the output), not on the buttons. The buttons are exactly what changes every Tuesday.", "url": "https://x.com/charl1sebastian/status/2117424339507146875"}, {"author_id": "2117214095552495616", "created_at": "2026-11-03T01:09:32.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117423899617141093"], "id": "2117423899617141093", "in_reply_to_user_id": "39125788", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 3, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117279363175739630", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@emollick If that's the belief, it explains a lot. But users build habits on these \"temporary\" products, so the churn costs real trust today.", "url": "https://x.com/messylinks/status/2117423899617141093"}, {"author_id": "1366194671504875521", "created_at": "2026-11-03T01:03:57.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117422495615881655"], "id": "2117422495615881655", "in_reply_to_user_id": "39125788", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 1, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117279363175739630", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@emollick 「本物のAGIまでのつなぎ」という前提が強いと、改善の優先順位が今のユーザーの困りごとから外れやすいのかもしれません。継続利用を決めるのは、結局いまの仕事がどれだけ安定して進むかですね。", "url": "https://x.com/Rachel_hkz/status/2117422495615881655"}, {"author_id": "1365086806903975937", "created_at": "2026-11-03T00:52:19.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117419569069617218"], "id": "2117419569069617218", "in_reply_to_user_id": "39125788", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 1, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117279363175739630", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@emollick So basically we all beta testers ATM", "url": "https://x.com/InfamousLetters/status/2117419569069617218"}, {"author_id": "2426422279", "created_at": "2026-11-03T00:43:31.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117417354317713822"], "id": "2117417354317713822", "in_reply_to_user_id": "39125788", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 1, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117279363175739630", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@emollick This explains a lot from the builder side. If the product is a bridge to fundraising, breaking changes are cheap for the lab and expensive for everyone building on top. It's why I now wrap every model call behind my own interface and assume the API will shift under me.", "url": "https://x.com/chengweiguang/status/2117417354317713822"}, {"author_id": "1904847916487106560", "created_at": "2026-11-03T00:43:00.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117417221970604196"], "id": "2117417221970604196", "in_reply_to_user_id": "39125788", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 1, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117279363175739630", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@emollick The customer may be storing years of work in a product the builder thinks of as temporary. That mismatch seems worth taking seriously.", "url": "https://x.com/wang_dx7909/status/2117417221970604196"}, {"author_id": "41185183", "created_at": "2026-11-03T00:41:32.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117416852716679601"], "id": "2117416852716679601", "in_reply_to_user_id": "39125788", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 2, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117279363175739630", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@emollick Products as a fundraising side quest. The changelog makes sense now.", "url": "https://x.com/brunopikler/status/2117416852716679601"}, {"author_id": "1707322478", "created_at": "2026-11-03T00:23:07.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117412220858438130"], "id": "2117412220858438130", "in_reply_to_user_id": "39125788", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 0, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117279363175739630", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@emollick AGI可以是终极目标，但用户不会一直为不成熟的产品买单。", "url": "https://x.com/whb0821/status/2117412220858438130"}, {"author_id": "2036898324330999808", "created_at": "2026-11-02T23:25:24.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117397695417729495"], "id": "2117397695417729495", "in_reply_to_user_id": "39125788", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 5, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117279363175739630", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@emollick explains why usage limits change every other week 😅", "url": "https://x.com/IA_makasi/status/2117397695417729495"}, {"author_id": "1217542539806478336", "created_at": "2026-11-02T23:17:55.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117395812082950268"], "id": "2117395812082950268", "in_reply_to_user_id": "39125788", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 2, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117279363175739630", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@emollick Legal teams feel those sudden changes most. A review protocol a lawyer has to defend can't shift because a model changed overnight. That's why the workflow around the model matters more than the model: a cited reason for every call, and a record of what ran on which documents.", "url": "https://x.com/DipoThompson/status/2117395812082950268"}, {"author_id": "14234967", "created_at": "2026-11-02T22:59:01.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117391057264804205"], "id": "2117391057264804205", "in_reply_to_user_id": "14210529", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 10, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117284610560131399", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@MFrancis107 @emollick Yeah it's why building products specifically aimed at developers and AI is not really a wise idea for commercial projects... Open source for sure, but not commercial", "url": "https://x.com/scottjla/status/2117391057264804205"}, {"author_id": "2086269595879723008", "created_at": "2026-11-02T22:32:59.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117384506034516129"], "id": "2117384506034516129", "in_reply_to_user_id": "39125788", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 2, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117279363175739630", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@emollick the products are a fundraising bridge until AGI makes products obsolete.\n\nso fleshbags are paying monthly to onboard their own replacement.\n\nhonestly the cleanest business model ever written.", "url": "https://x.com/AgentsOnlyAO/status/2117384506034516129"}, {"author_id": "2096242325748125696", "created_at": "2026-11-02T22:29:04.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117383516774170902"], "id": "2117383516774170902", "in_reply_to_user_id": "39125788", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 6, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117279363175739630", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@emollick this is the bit businesses building on these tools feel. model gets swapped or a feature changes overnight and the workflow breaks. i'd keep prompt + model behind one small layer and run a few saved test cases before switching anything", "url": "https://x.com/orionxaus/status/2117383516774170902"}, {"author_id": "1499198533106540546", "created_at": "2026-11-02T22:12:22.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117379314954187074"], "id": "2117379314954187074", "in_reply_to_user_id": "39125788", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 10, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117279363175739630", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@emollick Explains why every app update feels like it was shipped by someone halfway through packing boxes for a move.", "url": "https://x.com/ajutqs/status/2117379314954187074"}, {"author_id": "2110603562288062464", "created_at": "2026-11-02T21:51:34.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117374079301005485"], "id": "2117374079301005485", "in_reply_to_user_id": "39125788", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 54, "like_count": 1, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117279363175739630", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@emollick From the small business end it's the sudden changes that hurt most. Someone finally learns one screen, it moves, and they're back to doing it by hand.", "url": "https://x.com/thataibloke/status/2117374079301005485"}, {"author_id": "15645853", "created_at": "2026-11-02T21:45:09.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117372466456850930"], "id": "2117372466456850930", "in_reply_to_user_id": "39125788", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 4, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117279363175739630", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@emollick For a business the practical takeaway is to expect the product to change under you. Write down which version a workflow was tested on, keep a few real tasks to rerun after each update, and know who decides whether to keep using it.", "url": "https://x.com/dewyemi/status/2117372466456850930"}, {"author_id": "2116579414813065216", "created_at": "2026-11-02T21:36:12.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117370213721391435"], "id": "2117370213721391435", "in_reply_to_user_id": "39125788", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 5, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117279363175739630", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@emollick bit awkward for the bridge theory when the bridge did $17B last quarter. at some point the temporary thing is just the business", "url": "https://x.com/ContextWindowed/status/2117370213721391435"}, {"author_id": "1353415909918920704", "created_at": "2026-11-02T21:25:30.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117367521460580651"], "id": "2117367521460580651", "in_reply_to_user_id": "39125788", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 14, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117279363175739630", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@emollick This explains why products I discover and come to love one week keep disappearing the next lol. The only way to keep things relatively stable is to build your own skills/projects.", "url": "https://x.com/TimBaer8/status/2117367521460580651"}, {"author_id": "462161049", "created_at": "2026-11-02T21:22:27.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117366751944147180"], "id": "2117366751944147180", "in_reply_to_user_id": "39125788", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 4, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117279363175739630", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@emollick That explains a lot of the roadmap whiplash. But enterprise buyers price in whether you'll still be around and stable in three years. Labs that treat the product as temporary will keep losing deals to boring vendors with changelogs.", "url": "https://x.com/karnakr/status/2117366751944147180"}, {"author_id": "1728830169563922432", "created_at": "2026-11-02T21:17:59.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117365631242645987"], "id": "2117365631242645987", "in_reply_to_user_id": "39125788", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 8, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117279363175739630", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@emollick Temporary things have a way of becoming the architecture. Half the world still runs on someone's stopgap.", "url": "https://x.com/walkerspearson/status/2117365631242645987"}, {"author_id": "1717958141181050880", "created_at": "2026-11-02T21:16:41.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117365303009333489"], "id": "2117365303009333489", "in_reply_to_user_id": "1810488444512337920", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 3, "like_count": 1, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117291720702665008", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@akramcodez @emollick A) they need products to make money in the meantime, and B) data collection &amp; training", "url": "https://x.com/daquariusj2013/status/2117365303009333489"}, {"author_id": "54597398", "created_at": "2026-11-02T21:16:40.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117365299209281952"], "id": "2117365299209281952", "in_reply_to_user_id": "39125788", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 3, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117279363175739630", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@emollick if the labs treat products as a fundraising chore, whoever treats the product as the business gets to own the customer.", "url": "https://x.com/nigharsh/status/2117365299209281952"}, {"author_id": "4003735828", "created_at": "2026-11-02T20:40:30.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117356197330178379"], "id": "2117356197330178379", "in_reply_to_user_id": "39125788", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 1, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117279363175739630", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@emollick That framing explains a lot.", "url": "https://x.com/plaith_ai/status/2117356197330178379"}, {"author_id": "2116622308999876608", "created_at": "2026-11-02T20:14:53.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117349748629778757"], "id": "2117349748629778757", "in_reply_to_user_id": "39125788", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 1, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117279363175739630", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@emollick Explains a lot. Hard to build a stable workflow on a product its makers see as temporary. Best hedge for regular users: keep your prompts and processes in your own docs, not locked inside one app.", "url": "https://x.com/prompstoprofit/status/2117349748629778757"}, {"author_id": "1634838827180212228", "created_at": "2026-11-02T20:06:33.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117347651268321786"], "id": "2117347651268321786", "in_reply_to_user_id": "39125788", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 8, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117279363175739630", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@emollick you can feel it in the changelogs\nfeatures ship like experiments and get pulled like experiments\nthe people building real workflows on top are the ones paying for that belief", "url": "https://x.com/mukh_higgsfield/status/2117347651268321786"}], "includes": {"users": [{"id": "1687985018717478912", "name": "Charlie Sebastian", "username": "charl1sebastian"}, {"id": "2117214095552495616", "name": "messy", "username": "messylinks"}, {"id": "1366194671504875521", "name": "れいちぇる_Web制作出身のAI・Webアプリ開発者", "username": "Rachel_hkz"}, {"id": "1365086806903975937", "name": "SURD", "username": "InfamousLetters"}, {"id": "2426422279", "name": "Jack Cheng | AI indie builder", "username": "chengweiguang"}, {"id": "1904847916487106560", "name": "wangdonxin", "username": "wang_dx7909"}, {"id": "41185183", "name": "BPRICK", "username": "brunopikler"}, {"id": "1707322478", "name": "景哥｜AI增长与落地", "username": "whb0821"}, {"id": "2036898324330999808", "name": "Rémy IA Makasi", "username": "IA_makasi"}, {"id": "1217542539806478336", "name": "Dipo Thompson", "username": "DipoThompson"}, {"id": "14234967", "name": "Scott", "username": "scottjla"}, {"id": "2086269595879723008", "name": "Agents Only", "username": "AgentsOnlyAO"}, {"id": "2096242325748125696", "name": "OrionX", "username": "orionxaus"}, {"id": "1499198533106540546", "name": "Ajut Q", "username": "ajutqs"}, {"id": "2110603562288062464", "name": "PJ | That AI Bloke", "username": "thataibloke"}, {"id": "15645853", "name": "Josh Olayemi", "username": "dewyemi"}, {"id": "2116579414813065216", "name": "ContextWindowed", "username": "ContextWindowed"}, {"id": "1353415909918920704", "name": "Tim Baer", "username": "TimBaer8"}, {"id": "462161049", "name": "Koti Karna", "username": "karnakr"}, {"id": "1728830169563922432", "name": "Walker", "username": "walkerspearson"}, {"id": "1717958141181050880", "name": "daquariusjohnson2013", "username": "daquariusj2013"}, {"id": "54597398", "name": "Harsh Nigam", "username": "nigharsh"}, {"id": "4003735828", "name": "plaith.ai", "username": "plaith_ai"}, {"id": "2116622308999876608", "name": "AI Money Tools", "username": "prompstoprofit"}, {"id": "1634838827180212228", "name": "Mukhsin Mukhtorov", "username": "mukh_higgsfield"}]}, "meta": {"newest_id": "2117424339507146875", "next_token": "b26v89c19zqg8o3juzlyibh5f24ts2u7szigmamwargcd", "oldest_id": "2117347651268321786", "result_count": 25}}